    "en": {
      "summary": "Sarcoidosis can affect lungs, lymph nodes, skin and eyes. NHS: specialist diagnosis; many cases settle, some need treatment — never invent steroid doses. Emergency: sudden severe breathlessness, chest pain, new vision loss, or neurological deficits.",
